<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Mersal.Amendment</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Mersal.Amendment</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!--
    30.1 — the amend/cancel rules. PURE, with no I/O and no dependencies at all.

    It lives in its own library rather than inside orders-service or pharmacy-service because BOTH need the
    same answers, and design 46 §3's rule ("the amendable scope is whatever has not been consumed") is one
    rule about two shapes of line. Two implementations would be two chances to disagree about whether a
    partly-dispensed line may be cancelled — and the disagreement would surface as a beneficiary who was
    refused at one counter and served at another.

    The reason vocabulary lives here too, as the SINGLE canonical source. Both services seed it into their
    own table (orders 0013, pharmacy 0013) so the FK is real and a cancellation never depends on another
    service being reachable; AmendmentReasonSeedTests reads both migrations and fails the build if either
    copy drifts from this list.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The Tests directory is its own project; without this the library compiles the tests into itself. -->
    <Compile Remove="Tests/**/*.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
